results.model_answer:
According to the Customs Agent Licensing Rules, 2016, the Licensing Authority can issue a show-cause notice to a customs agent and impose a penalty or revoke the license if the customs agent:

(1) Violates any provision of the Rules or any condition of the license;
(2) Is negligent, dilatory or incompetent in performing duties; 
(3) Behaves in an discourteous manner with customs officers;
(4) Fails to cooperate with customs authorities in investigating any misdeclaration by the agent's client.

The Licensing Authority can revoke the license and impose a fine in such cases, after providing the customs agent an opportunity to explain.

